        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "360ea6f6-50cf-3999-b2b3-db9204fca4f9",
                "word": "reliquaire",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5d2c405f-4e8f-400e-9d13-b152579ee9b8",
                        "entry_id": "360ea6f6-50cf-3999-b2b3-db9204fca4f9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "reliquaires"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f90fdf79-b979-3c66-8373-2bdc10f65735",
                        "entry_id": "360ea6f6-50cf-3999-b2b3-db9204fca4f9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sorte de boîte, de coffret de forme variable, où l’on conserve des reliques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Funéraire"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28e59655-211e-47b2-ae66-06ff94212581",
                                "sense_id": "f90fdf79-b979-3c66-8373-2bdc10f65735",
                                "text": "Et que proposez-vous pour gage ?\n– Ce reliquaire, qui contient un fragment de la vraie croix, rapporté du monastère du mont Carmel, dit le pèlerin en tirant de sa poitrine une petite boîte d’ivoire et en se signant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cef2daf-7029-43af-9855-61319b7c1aa1",
                                "sense_id": "f90fdf79-b979-3c66-8373-2bdc10f65735",
                                "text": "En 1708, le deuxième dimanche de Carême, les reliques de sainte Gaudence, envoyées de Rome pour la paroisse d’Hauteville, ont été enchâssées dans un reliquaire de bois doré dans l'église de cette ville par M. le doyen de Rethel avec solennité."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b46f2ea-df88-4be6-a6a2-feaf2972f6c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "360ea6f6-50cf-3999-b2b3-db9204fca4f9",
                        "source_sense_id": "f90fdf79-b979-3c66-8373-2bdc10f65735",
                        "source_sense_description": "contenant à relique",
                        "target_lang_word": "Reliquienschrein",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64a79f1a-0890-4f74-98ec-a9800d2bd22f",
                        "source_entry_id": "360ea6f6-50cf-3999-b2b3-db9204fca4f9",
                        "source_sense_id": "f90fdf79-b979-3c66-8373-2bdc10f65735",
                        "source_sense_description": "contenant à relique",
                        "target_lang_word": "reliquary",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reliquary",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c237da11-c12f-3663-9a3e-ceea07d91b27",
                                        "entry_id": "8ab1f460-5e14-3b1d-b5ea-ab2fc131aab6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A container to hold or display religious relics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dc10089-9a04-4c10-90be-fece3994cb35",
                                                "sense_id": "c237da11-c12f-3663-9a3e-ceea07d91b27",
                                                "text": "“… There is an ivory virgin of the fourteenth century. I once found a buyer for that piece, but the old boy would not sell it.[…]The other piece—the one that concerns us—is known as the Borgia reliquary.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc7e4eef-0b5d-431f-9295-923c64e89970",
                                                "sense_id": "c237da11-c12f-3663-9a3e-ceea07d91b27",
                                                "text": "And whether you think of those little cans as intellectual puzzles or reliquaries or scams, there are surprises inside."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df2a8d72-52ae-3af7-9987-153bccafba61",
                                        "entry_id": "8ab1f460-5e14-3b1d-b5ea-ab2fc131aab6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object that sustains the memory of past people or events."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3273aad-08bc-3625-a821-80ceaa61c010",
                                        "entry_id": "8ab1f460-5e14-3b1d-b5ea-ab2fc131aab6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who owes a balance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "12f409c9-c95d-4f64-8a17-430ac58fb963",
                        "source_entry_id": "360ea6f6-50cf-3999-b2b3-db9204fca4f9",
                        "source_sense_id": "f90fdf79-b979-3c66-8373-2bdc10f65735",
                        "source_sense_description": "contenant à relique",
                        "target_lang_word": "shrine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shrine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bc95d6d-07c1-374e-8632-d3076a1d6e6f",
                                        "entry_id": "3deaaebf-8a61-3142-868d-247c6e4ca5ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A holy or sacred place dedicated to a specific deity, ancestor, hero, martyr, saint, or similar figure of awe and respect, at which said figure is venerated or worshipped."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a9dc771-0adb-4549-87ef-84cc8f1e732f",
                                                "sense_id": "5bc95d6d-07c1-374e-8632-d3076a1d6e6f",
                                                "text": "Entering the tunnel, we pass a small shrine above our heads which contains a statue of St Barbara, the patron saint of tunnellers. It is traditional to have such shrines on every tunnel site."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8fbe338-0b26-3091-85f9-700c604ade1f",
                                        "entry_id": "3deaaebf-8a61-3142-868d-247c6e4ca5ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A case, box, or receptacle, especially one in which are deposited sacred relics, as the bones of a saint."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5bdc4295-f268-3aad-9e54-f036735c512c",
                                        "entry_id": "3deaaebf-8a61-3142-868d-247c6e4ca5ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place or object hallowed from its history or associations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cbf4e59-d0dd-4b4d-ac8a-3b6f9ded2a0a",
                                                "sense_id": "5bdc4295-f268-3aad-9e54-f036735c512c",
                                                "text": "a shrine of art"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shrine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f852e74-6530-3d60-8f1f-d18278e467ce",
                                        "entry_id": "f3fad8c5-d65a-3cde-8a64-f32174597955",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enshrine; to place reverently, as if in a shrine."
